{
  "assembly_notes": "Wheeled hydraulic floor (trolley) jack. One rigid jack_chassis root carries the side frames, the ram cylinder, the front roller stubs and the rear station brackets. The lift_arm is a REVOLUTE (+x) child of the chassis at the rear pivot and is the only independent lift joint; the saddle_head is a REVOLUTE (+x) child of the arm nose mimicking the arm at multiplier -1, which is the real parallel-linkage that keeps a floor-jack head level through the whole lift. The ram piston is an independent PRISMATIC child of the chassis sliding inside a real cylinder bore (a prismatic cannot mimic a revolute, and the source authors it independently too). pump_input is a REVOLUTE (+x) lever at the rear. Two front_roller wheels are CONTINUOUS (+x); rear_station_count wheel_station parts carry the rear, each either a swivel caster (REVOLUTE kingpin about +z plus a CONTINUOUS wheel) or a rigid roller (CONTINUOUS only). Four component slots vary without touching the mechanism: saddle_head, chassis_style, pump_drive and wheel_station. chassis_len_m, chassis_width_m and arm_reach_ratio are independent continuous parameters deriving arm length, lift height, wheel track, station pitch, ram station and handle length; palette is non-core.",
